From 6eb77581309be94b8f2eb2b983d68e8bc2ad364b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:04:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] port b1daa17a: serve: STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1 captures a
 finished request's conversation beside the slots

Renamed for v0.2.12: STRATA_PARK_ASYNC is upstream's own, different park
(f73b3c86, #3779: a VRAM stage copy and a background host copy), so ours
is STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE=1, with STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE_THREADS=1 (was
STRATA_PARK_THREADS) and STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE_VERIFY=1 (was
STRATA_PARK_ASYNC_VERIFY).  Everything stays opt-in; with the three
unset nothing changes.

Both set: ours runs and upstream's stays off.  conversation_park_capture_env()
(conversation_snapshot.hpp) is read by upstream's park_async_on() in the
core and by park_async_env() in generate.cpp, and the engine prints
"STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1 is ignored: STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE is set" once at
start.  Chosen over refusing because upstream's stage, VRAM slots and
pending tokens are process-wide state of the serve thread: a capture on
other threads beside them would race, and a config that still carries
STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1 (production.json does) keeps the measured park
instead of silently getting the 1.5 GB VRAM one.

Rebased onto upstream's park_source / ParkSource (#2526):
- PARK_CAPTURE_THREADS: the stage-parallel capture replaces the stage 0
  save and the later-stage loop in park_source when there is a split
  (upstream's STRATA_CKPT_POOL storage and park_drops move-in only run
  without one); the old order otherwise, re-indented under else.
- park_capture_start/take/drop/sync/job/discard (were park_async_*):
  placed before pipe_drain; take_reuse_for(live) instead of
  take_reuse() (#1503), retain(..., live) for the kept pages,
  conversation_checkpoint_join(nullptr) before a capture thread copies
  `checks` (STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC), and park_worth (park gain) in the
  decision.  Upstream's borrow branch drops a running capture and parks
  synchronously beside the guarded donor.
- ParkThreads uses StageThreads::spread_current_thread() and names its
  threads strata-park (upstream already made the CPU spread public; no
  spread_engine_thread refactor).
- ConversationCapture gained own_copies/plain(): any non-plain capture
  copies on its own thread through StagedCopy and never touches the
  process-wide CKPT_ASYNC / CKPT_GATHER / PARK_ASYNC stages (dev_tag 0,
  no pending tokens); plain() is upstream's code exactly.  The VERIFY
  reference capture uses own_copies for the same reason.
- conversation_checkpoint_same / conversation_image_same leave the VRAM
  copy tags (dev_tag) and pending tokens out, like capacities.

No server.py hunk in b1daa17a (the subject's "serve:" is the engine's
serve loop).  Docs not added (none in the source commit).

(cherry picked from commit b1daa17ab0d7c1bd39524eb19ef266e7aa9487ff)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
